# Slack Message Formatting

## mrkdwn basics

| Style          | Syntax          |
|----------------|-----------------|
| Bold           | `*text*`        |
| Italic         | `_text_`        |
| Strikethrough  | `~text~`        |
| Inline code    | `` `text` ``    |
| Code block     | fenced with backticks |
| Quote          | `> text`        |
| Bullet list    | `• item` or `- item` |

## Links

- `<https://example.com>` renders the URL itself.
- `<https://example.com|Click here>` renders "Click here" as a link.
- Link to a user: `<@U1234567890>`; to a channel: `<#C1234567890>`.

## Emoji

Use shortcodes without colons in `reactions.add` (`name: "tada"`), and with colons in message text: `:white_check_mark:`, `:warning:`.

## Escaping user-provided text

Escape `&` -> `&amp;`, `<` -> `&lt;`, `>` -> `&gt;` so user content is not parsed as formatting.

## Block Kit examples

### Section with text and fields

```json
{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "section",
      "text": {
        "type": "mrkdwn",
        "text": "Deploy finished for *api-server*."
      },
      "fields": [
        { "type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*Status:*\n:white_check_mark: success" },
        { "type": "mrkdwn", "text": "*Duration:*\n2m 14s" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "context",
      "elements": [
        { "type": "mrkdwn", "text": "Triggered by <@U1234567890>" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Section with an action button

```json
{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "section",
      "text": { "type": "mrkdwn", "text": "Approve the release?" },
      "accessory": {
        "type": "button",
        "text": { "type": "plain_text", "text": "Approve" },
        "action_id": "approve_release",
        "value": "release-1.2.3"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Note: buttons are interactive; the bot must handle interactions/events for them to be useful. For one-way notifications, prefer plain `text` or `section` blocks.

